/-!
# VIII08R — existence from profile regularity alone, and full `(b, v)` uniqueness

* **Bound witnesses.** Continuity of `q`, `r` on `U` and compactness of `K = [0, 1/3]` produce
  `Aq, Ar ≥ 0` with `|q| ≤ Aq`, `|r| ≤ Ar` on `K`.  These are witnesses of the *same* theorem that
  states existence, so the main root below assumes only profile regularity.
* **Pair uniqueness.** If `b₀ ∈ MagClass 3` and `v₀ ∈ VClass 3` solve the actual equations with the
  same profiles `(j, q, r)`, then `b₀ = b_s` and `v₀ = v_s` on `I`.  The `b` part is
  `mag_eqOn_of_Lmag_eq`; the `v` part differentiates the (proved) `Dell` identity for `v_s` to get
  the common derivative source and applies the inherited `VIII04.v_unique` — never assuming `v` equal,
  never assuming an energy/endpoint condition beyond the class itself.
-/

